=== FINDING (contract defect, found during the run) ===
34.9-LIVE-GATE.md item 5 instructs: set altNileBin to `public/bin/x64/darwin/nile`.
That is a REPO-RELATIVE path. The sidecar spawns runners with
cwd=/Users/graysonmitchell/Projects/GameLib/src-tauri, so the relative path resolves to
src-tauri/public/bin/x64/darwin/nile, which does not exist -> ENOENT
("no such file or directory"). Confirmed:
  $ ls src-tauri/public/bin/x64/darwin/nile  -> No such file or directory
  $ ls public/bin/x64/darwin/nile            -> exists, Mach-O 64-bit x86_64
  $ ./public/bin/x64/darwin/nile --version   -> "1.1.2 Will A. Zeppeli", exit 0 (Rosetta OK)
This is a defect in the CONTRACT's wording, not in the product: the Settings field is a
file picker (PathSelectionBox type="file"), which always yields an absolute path, so no
real user can reach this state. Item 5 is re-run with the absolute path; the override
MECHANISM under test is unchanged.

Side effect observed and consistent with source: the invalid path caused
AltNileBin.tsx's `nileVer === 'invalid'` branch to display "Invalid" and then auto-clear
altNileBin after 3000ms. config.json confirmed to hold no alt*Bin key afterwards, i.e.
the app self-restored to the default nested path. Not scored as item 5's restoration
check -- that must be a deliberate set-then-clear, not an error-triggered revert.

