=== FINDING (pre-existing, not caused by 34.9): file picker fails silently and intermittently ===
First picker attempt in this session produced a system beep, would not navigate, and committed
NOTHING -- config.json afterwards held altNileBin = '' (that empty value came from the earlier
paste attempt's invalid-path auto-clear, not from the picker). A later attempt in a restarted
app succeeded normally. So the picker is INTERMITTENT, not categorically broken -- an earlier
reading of this transcript that called it "confirmed broken" would be overstating the evidence.
What makes it undiagnosable is electronStub.showOpenDialog's error handling:
    catch (error) { console.warn(...); return { canceled: true, filePaths: [] } }
Every failure mode -- timeout, unknown channel, permission denial -- is converted into a value
byte-identical to a genuine user cancel, and the sole diagnostic is a console.warn from the
sidecar, whose stdout IS the RPC pipe and therefore reaches no readable sink. openDialogCallback
then returns false, `if (selectedPath)` is false, onPathChange is never called, and the UI simply
keeps its placeholder. There is no channel in which this failure is visible to anyone.
Out of scope for Phase 34.9's verdict: the defect is in the Phase 30/31 dialog port, is
independent of runner packaging, and no scored item depends on the picker (item 5's mechanism is
getNileBin()'s branch, reachable by any means of setting the value).

