=== SCORING: launch ordinal 5 -- ITEM 4, Electron PACKAGED : FAIL ===
`pnpm dist:mac` DID NOT COMPLETE. electron-builder aborted during adhoc code signing:

  ⨯ Command failed: codesign --sign - --force --timestamp --options runtime \
      --entitlements build/entitlements.mac.plist \
      dist/mac-arm64/GameLib.app/Contents/Resources/app.asar.unpacked/build/bin/arm64/\
      darwin/gogdl/_internal/Python.framework/Python
    .../Python.framework/Python: replacing existing signature
    .../Python.framework/Python: bundle format is ambiguous (could be app or framework)
    failedTask=build

No `pnpm verify:runner-bundle` run was possible and no packaged app could be inspected, so
item 4's two evidence requirements are both unreachable. Item 4 is a FAIL, not NOT ATTEMPTED:
the attempt was made under satisfied preconditions and the product failed it.

--- ROOT CAUSE, established causally rather than inferred ---
Phase 34.9's onedir trees each contain a `Python.framework` bundle (present in ALL THREE
runners; 3 symlinks each in source). vite's copyDir (publicDir -> outDir, electron.vite.config.ts)
has no symlink branch -- it statSync()s through links and copyFileSync()s -- so every framework
symlink becomes a real file/directory in build/, and from there in the packaged app:

  source  public/.../Python.framework/  Python -> Versions/Current/Python   (symlink)
                                        Resources -> Versions/Current/Resources (symlink)
                                        Versions/Current -> 3.14            (symlink)
  packaged dist/.../Python.framework/   Python    = real 5,454,496-byte FILE
                                        Resources = real DIRECTORY
                                        Versions/Current = real DIRECTORY

Apple's framework layout requires Versions/Current to be a symlink; without it codesign cannot
classify the bundle. Discriminating experiment, ONE variable (cp -R vs cp -RL on the SAME
source framework), same codesign invocation electron-builder used:

  A-symlinked     Versions/Current is symlink        -> codesign exit 0, signs cleanly
  B-dereferenced  Versions/Current is real directory -> codesign exit 1,
                                                        "bundle format is ambiguous"

=> The dereferencing is the cause, and it is a Phase 34.9 regression: before this phase the
darwin runners were flat single-file binaries containing no framework and no symlinks, so this
code path could not be reached.

--- CORRECTION TO AN EARLIER READING IN THIS SAME RUN ---
Earlier in this session the symlink dereferencing was examined and recorded as "functionally
benign so far", on the strength of `codesign --verify --deep` exiting 0 against the runner's
INNER BINARY (.../gogdl/gogdl). That check was aimed at the wrong target: it never signed the
Python.framework BUNDLE, which is what actually fails. The benign reading was wrong and is
superseded by this item's result. Recorded here rather than silently overwritten, because the
false-comfort check is itself the lesson: verifying a nearby artifact is not verifying the one
the toolchain will touch.

--- TRAP: stale artifacts survive a failed build ---
dist/GameLib-0.7.0-macOS-arm64.dmg and .zip EXIST and look like this build's output. They are
dated 2026-07-21, three weeks stale and pre-34.9, and contain the OLD FLAT binaries
(gogdl = one 11,218,928-byte file; zero `_internal` onedir entries in the archive). Only
dist/mac-arm64/ was cleared before this build. Anyone checking "did dist:mac produce a dmg?"
would get a yes from a pre-34.9 artifact. THIS BUILD PRODUCED NO DISTRIBUTABLE ARTIFACT.
The dist/mac-arm64/GameLib.app directory is a partial, unsigned tree abandoned mid-signing.

